-- Rules of Court 2021 (Singapore), G.N. No. S 914/2021, current version as at 5 November 2026.
-- ORDER 19 (part roc4), DIVISION 2 -- APPEAL FROM DISTRICT COURT AND MAGISTRATE'S COURT TO GENERAL DIVISION
-- (rules 13 to 23), LAYER 1: the law, objectively.
-- Source: a plain-text rendering made by a converter script from Singapore Statutes Online.
-- It is not the official text, and nothing here has been checked against the official text.
--
-- HOW TO READ A RESULT, and the time seams: as in roc4-order-19-div-1.l4 (imported; its helper
-- `o 19 r 8(3) the filing and the service are done by the last day` is called here).
-- Each function is named for the provision's own proposition (the duty, the bar, the power), so that JUST FALSE says
-- "the text says the provision does not apply or is not met" and NOTHING says "the text does not answer".
-- In this Division "the lower Court" is the District Court or the Magistrate's Court against whose judgment the appeal is brought (rule 13(2)).

-- ===========================================================================
§ `Order 19 -- Division 2 -- Appeal from District Court and Magistrate's Court to General Division`
-- ===========================================================================

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 13 -- scope of this Division`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:2350 | 13. —(1) This Division applies to appeals to the General Division against any judgment of the District Court or Magistrate’s Court given — ( a )
-- src:2351 | in a trial of an originating claim, including a case where judgment is given or the action is dismissed at trial because one or more parties are absent; [S 206/2022 wef 01/04/2022]
-- src:2352 | ( b )
-- src:2353 | after damages are assessed or accounts are taken by a District Judge; or
-- src:2354 | ( c )
-- src:2355 | in an application for a committal order for contempt of court.
-- src:2356 | (2) In this Division, “lower Court” means the District Court or Magistrate’s Court (as the case may be) against which judgment an appeal is brought or being brought.
@ref O 19 r 13 (src:2350-2356)
GIVEN judgment IS A `o 19 r 1 judgment appealed against`
      `the appeal is to the General Division` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 19 r 13(1) this Division applies to an appeal against a judgment of the District Court or Magistrate's Court` MEANS
    IF   `the appeal is to the General Division`
     AND (   judgment's `o 19 r 1 court that gave it` EQUALS `Magistrate's Court`
          OR judgment's `o 19 r 1 court that gave it` EQUALS `District Court`)
     AND (   (    judgment's `o 19 r 1 what it was given in` EQUALS `o 19 r 3(a) a trial`
              AND judgment's `o 19 r 1 the proceedings began with` EQUALS `Originating claim`)
          OR (    judgment's `o 19 r 1 what it was given in` EQUALS `o 19 r 3(a) a case where judgment is given or the action is dismissed at trial because one or more parties are absent`
              AND judgment's `o 19 r 1 the proceedings began with` EQUALS `Originating claim`)
          OR (    judgment's `o 19 r 1 what it was given in` EQUALS `o 19 r 3(b) after damages are assessed or accounts are taken`
              AND judgment's `o 19 r 1 damages or accounts by a District Judge`)
          OR judgment's `o 19 r 1 what it was given in` EQUALS `o 19 r 3(c) an application for a committal order for contempt of court`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): paragraph (1) names three kinds of judgment of the District Court or Magistrate's Court and does not say "only"

@ref O 19 r 13(2) (src:2356)
GIVEN court IS A `Court level`
      `an appeal against its judgment is brought or being brought` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 19 r 13(2) a court is the lower Court` MEANS
    IF (court EQUALS `District Court` OR court EQUALS `Magistrate's Court`) AND `an appeal against its judgment is brought or being brought`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“lower Court” means the District Court or Magistrate’s Court (as the case may be) against which judgment an appeal is brought or being brought"

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 14 -- bringing of appeal`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

`o 19 r 14(1) the period for the notice of appeal` MEANS Period WITH
    `period length` IS 14
    `period unit` IS Days
    `period direction` IS `After the anchor`

-- src:2358 | 14. —(1) A party who intends to appeal to the General Division against the judgment of a lower Court must file and serve on all parties who have an interest in the appeal a notice of appeal in Form 35 within 14 days after the date of the judgment. (2) The General Division may extend the time for filing and serving the notice of appeal on the appellant’s application made at any time, and the lower Court may extend the time for filing and serving the notice of appeal if the appellant applies for such extension before the time expires.
@ref O 19 r 14 (src:2358)
GIVEN `the notice of appeal is in Form 35` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice is served on all parties who have an interest in the appeal` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the notice of appeal is filed` IS A DATE
      `the date the notice of appeal is served` IS A DATE
      `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act` IS A DATE
      `o 3 r 4 the last day as extended or shortened` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 19 r 14(1) the notice of appeal is filed and served as required` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the notice of appeal is in Form 35` AND `the notice is served on all parties who have an interest in the appeal`)
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must file and serve on all parties who have an interest in the appeal a notice of appeal in Form 35"
        IF NOT (`o 19 r 8(3) the filing and the service are done by the last day` `the date the notice of appeal is filed` `the date the notice of appeal is served` `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act` `o 3 r 4 the last day as extended or shortened`)
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "within 14 days after the date of the judgment" -- outside a period the text fixes in its own words
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

@ref O 19 r 14(2) (src:2358)
GIVEN `the appellant applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 19 r 14(2) the General Division may extend the time for filing and serving the notice of appeal` MEANS
    IF `the appellant applies`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "on the appellant’s application made at any time" -- an "on application" that is not met, read as "upon"

@ref O 19 r 14(2) (src:2358)
GIVEN `the appellant applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the appellant applies before the time expires` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 19 r 14(2) the lower Court may extend the time for filing and serving the notice of appeal` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the appellant applies`)
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the appellant applies for such extension" -- an "if" that is not met
        IF `the appellant applies before the time expires`
            THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the lower Court may extend the time ... if the appellant applies for such extension before the time expires" -- an "if" and a time that is not met

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 15 -- permission to appeal`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

`o 19 r 15(1) the period for the application for permission to the lower Court` MEANS Period WITH
    `period length` IS 14
    `period unit` IS Days
    `period direction` IS `After the anchor`

`o 19 r 15(2) the period for the application for permission to the General Division` MEANS Period WITH
    `period length` IS 14
    `period unit` IS Days
    `period direction` IS `After the anchor`

`o 19 r 15(3) the period for the notice of appeal after permission is granted` MEANS Period WITH
    `period length` IS 14
    `period unit` IS Days
    `period direction` IS `After the anchor`

-- src:2360 | 15. —(1) Where permission to appeal is required, a party must apply for such permission from the lower Court and serve the application on all parties who have an interest in the appeal within 14 days after the date of the judgment. (2) Where the lower Court does not grant permission to appeal, the party may apply to the General Division for such permission and must serve the application on all parties who have an interest in the appeal within 14 days after the date of the lower Court’s decision not to grant permission.
-- src:2361 | (3) Where permission to appeal is granted, the applicant must file and serve on all parties who have an interest in the appeal the notice of appeal in Form 35 within 14 days after the date of the decision granting permission.
-- src:2362 | (4) The General Division may extend the time for filing and serving an application for permission to appeal made at any time, and the lower Court may extend the time for filing and serving an application for permission to appeal if the application for such extension is made before the time expires.
@ref O 19 r 15 (src:2360-2362)
GIVEN `permission to appeal is required` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application is made to the lower Court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application is served on all parties who have an interest in the appeal` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the application to the lower Court is made` IS A DATE
      `the date the application is served` IS A DATE
      `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act` IS A DATE
      `o 3 r 4 the last day as extended or shortened` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 19 r 15(1) the application for permission to the lower Court is made and served as required` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`permission to appeal is required`)
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where permission to appeal is required" -- a "where" that is not met
        IF NOT (`the application is made to the lower Court`)
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a party must apply for such permission from the lower Court" -- the application went to another court
        IF NOT (`the application is served on all parties who have an interest in the appeal`)
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "serve the application on all parties who have an interest in the appeal"
        IF NOT (`o 19 r 8(3) the filing and the service are done by the last day` `the date the application to the lower Court is made` `the date the application is served` `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act` `o 3 r 4 the last day as extended or shortened`)
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "within 14 days after the date of the judgment" -- outside a period the text fixes in its own words
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

@ref O 19 r 15(2) (src:2360)
GIVEN `the lower Court does not grant permission to appeal` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application is served on all parties who have an interest in the appeal` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the application to the General Division is made` IS A DATE
      `the date the application is served` IS A DATE
      `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act` IS A DATE
      `o 3 r 4 the last day as extended or shortened` IS A MAYBE DATE
