-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 19 -- page limits`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

DECLARE `o 19 r 19(1) document` IS ONE OF
    `o 19 r 19(1)(a) the appellant's Case`
    `o 19 r 19(1)(b) the respondent's Case`
    `o 19 r 19(1)(c) the appellant's Reply`

DECLARE `o 19 r 19(2) document` IS ONE OF
    `o 19 r 19(2)(a) the appellant's core bundle of documents (excluding the written judgment or grounds of decision of the lower Court and the extracted order of the lower Court)`
    `o 19 r 19(2)(b) the respondent's core bundle of documents`
    `o 19 r 19(2)(c) the second core bundle`

-- The limits, as a ruler: Case 35, Case 35, Reply 20; core bundles 55, 35, 25.
-- src:2468 | 19. —(1) The appellant’s Case, the respondent’s Case and the appellant’s Reply (if any) are subject to the following page limits, unless the General Division otherwise orders: ( a )
-- src:2469 | appellant’s Case — 35 pages;
-- src:2470 | ( b )
-- src:2471 | respondent’s Case — 35 pages;
-- src:2472 | ( c )
-- src:2473 | appellant’s Reply — 20 pages.
-- src:2474 | (2) The appellant’s core bundle of documents (excluding the written judgment or grounds of decision of the lower Court and the extracted order of the lower Court), the respondent’s core bundle of documents and the second core bundle are subject to the following page limits, unless the General Division otherwise orders: ( a )
-- src:2475 | appellant’s core bundle of documents (excluding the written judgment or grounds of decision of the lower Court and the extracted order of the lower Court) — 55 pages;
-- src:2476 | ( b )
-- src:2477 | respondent’s core bundle of documents — 35 pages;
-- src:2478 | ( c )
-- src:2479 | second core bundle — 25 pages.
-- src:2480 | (3) The General Division may allow the page limit mentioned in paragraphs (1) and (2) to be exceeded — ( a )
-- src:2481 | in special circumstances; and
-- src:2482 | ( b )
-- src:2483 | unless the General Division otherwise orders under paragraph (4), upon the payment of the fees and additional fees prescribed for the filing of pages in excess of the page limit.
-- src:2484 | (4) The General Division may upon application waive, refund, defer or apportion the payment of the fees mentioned in paragraph (3)( b ).
@ref O 19 r 19 (src:2468-2484)
GIVEN document IS A `o 19 r 19(1) document`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`o 19 r 19(1) the page limit` MEANS
    CONSIDER document
    WHEN `o 19 r 19(1)(a) the appellant's Case` THEN 35
    WHEN `o 19 r 19(1)(b) the respondent's Case` THEN 35
    WHEN `o 19 r 19(1)(c) the appellant's Reply` THEN 20

@ref O 19 r 19(1) (src:2468-2473)
GIVEN document IS A `o 19 r 19(1) document`
      pages IS A NUMBER
      `the General Division otherwise orders` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 19 r 19(1) the document is within the page limit` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the General Division otherwise orders`
            THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "unless the General Division otherwise orders" -- the order's limit is not in these sources
        IF pages AT MOST `o 19 r 19(1) the page limit` document
            THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "are subject to the following page limits ... appellant’s Case — 35 pages; respondent’s Case — 35 pages; appellant’s Reply — 20 pages"

@ref O 19 r 19(2) (src:2474-2479)
GIVEN document IS A `o 19 r 19(2) document`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`o 19 r 19(2) the page limit` MEANS
    CONSIDER document
    WHEN `o 19 r 19(2)(a) the appellant's core bundle of documents (excluding the written judgment or grounds of decision of the lower Court and the extracted order of the lower Court)` THEN 55
    WHEN `o 19 r 19(2)(b) the respondent's core bundle of documents` THEN 35
    WHEN `o 19 r 19(2)(c) the second core bundle` THEN 25

@ref O 19 r 19(2) (src:2474-2479)
GIVEN document IS A `o 19 r 19(2) document`
      pages IS A NUMBER
      `the General Division otherwise orders` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 19 r 19(2) the document is within the page limit` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the General Division otherwise orders`
            THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "unless the General Division otherwise orders" -- the order's limit is not in these sources
        IF pages AT MOST `o 19 r 19(2) the page limit` document
            THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "are subject to the following page limits ... 55 pages; ... 35 pages; ... 25 pages"

@ref O 19 r 19(3) (src:2480-2483)
GIVEN `there are special circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 19 r 19(3)(a) the General Division may allow the page limit to be exceeded` MEANS
    IF `there are special circumstances`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is given "in special circumstances"

@ref O 19 r 19(3)(b) (src:2482-2483)
GIVEN `the General Division allows the page limit to be exceeded` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the General Division otherwise orders under paragraph (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 19 r 19(3)(b) the fees and additional fees for the pages in excess are payable` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the General Division allows the page limit to be exceeded`)
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may allow the page limit ... to be exceeded ... upon the payment of the fees" -- an "upon" that is not met
        IF `the General Division otherwise orders under paragraph (4)`
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the General Division otherwise orders under paragraph (4)"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- The fee is the Fourth Schedule's (roc12): the amount payable is that input when the fees are payable.
@ref O 19 r 19(3)(b) (src:2482-2483)
GIVEN `the General Division allows the page limit to be exceeded` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the General Division otherwise orders under paragraph (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `sch 4 the fee for this document` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`o 19 r 19(3)(b) the amount payable for the pages in excess` MEANS
    IF `o 19 r 19(3)(b) the fees and additional fees for the pages in excess are payable` `the General Division allows the page limit to be exceeded` `the General Division otherwise orders under paragraph (4)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST `sch 4 the fee for this document`
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the fees are not payable here, or have been waived, refunded, deferred or apportioned, and the amount then is not in these sources

@ref O 19 r 19(4) (src:2484)
GIVEN `a party applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 19 r 19(4) the General Division may waive, refund, defer or apportion the payment of the fees` MEANS
    IF `a party applies`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "upon application" -- an "upon" that is not met

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 20 -- payment out of security for costs and release of undertaking`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:2486 | 20. —(1) This Rule applies without the need for an order from the Court. (2) Where costs are payable by the appellant to the respondent under any order made by the General Division, the security for costs provided under Rule 16 must be paid to the respondent towards the costs ordered and the balance (if any) of the security must be paid to the appellant.
-- src:2487 | (3) Where no costs are payable by the appellant to the respondent under any order made by the General Division, the security for costs provided under Rule 16 must be paid to the appellant and the appellant’s solicitor is released from any undertaking as to the costs for the appeal.
@ref O 19 r 20 (src:2486-2487)
GIVEN `the Court has made an order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 19 r 20(1) an order from the Court is needed for this Rule to apply` MEANS
    JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This Rule applies without the need for an order from the Court" -- whether or not the Court has made one

@ref O 19 r 20(2) (src:2486)
GIVEN `the costs payable by the appellant to the respondent under an order made by the General Division` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 19 r 20(2) the security for costs must be paid to the respondent towards the costs ordered` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the costs payable by the appellant to the respondent under an order made by the General Division`
    WHEN JUST costs THEN
        IF costs GREATER THAN 0
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where costs are payable by the appellant to the respondent" -- none are payable
    WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where costs are payable by the appellant to the respondent" -- none are payable

-- The amount paid to the respondent is the smaller of the costs ordered and the security; the balance goes to the appellant.
@ref O 19 r 20(2) (src:2486)
GIVEN `the security for costs provided under Rule 16` IS A NUMBER
      `the costs payable by the appellant to the respondent under an order made by the General Division` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`o 19 r 20(2) the amount of the security paid to the respondent` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the costs payable by the appellant to the respondent under an order made by the General Division`
    WHEN JUST costs THEN
        BRANCH
            IF costs AT MOST 0
                THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): no costs are payable, so paragraph (3) applies
            IF costs AT MOST `the security for costs provided under Rule 16`
                THEN JUST costs
            OTHERWISE JUST `the security for costs provided under Rule 16`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): no costs are payable, so paragraph (3) applies

@ref O 19 r 20(2) (src:2486)
GIVEN `the security for costs provided under Rule 16` IS A NUMBER
      `the costs payable by the appellant to the respondent under an order made by the General Division` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`o 19 r 20(2) the balance of the security paid to the appellant` MEANS
    CONSIDER `o 19 r 20(2) the amount of the security paid to the respondent` `the security for costs provided under Rule 16` `the costs payable by the appellant to the respondent under an order made by the General Division`
    WHEN JUST paid THEN JUST (`the security for costs provided under Rule 16` MINUS paid)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): no costs are payable, so paragraph (3) applies

@ref O 19 r 20(3) (src:2487)
GIVEN `the costs payable by the appellant to the respondent under an order made by the General Division` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 19 r 20(3) the security for costs must be paid to the appellant and the appellant's solicitor is released from any undertaking` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the costs payable by the appellant to the respondent under an order made by the General Division`
    WHEN JUST costs THEN
        IF costs GREATER THAN 0
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where no costs are payable by the appellant to the respondent" -- some are payable
        ELSE JUST TRUE
    WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST TRUE

